---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { businessLd } from '../../schema';
import { SITE } from '../../site';
import hero from '../../assets/images/NatalieHammondDressage-25.jpg';
---

<Page
  title="Dressage Boarding in St. Louis, Missouri"
  heading="Dressage Boarding in St. Louis"
  eyebrow="Boarding"
  lede={`Boarding for horses in training with Natalie Hammond at ${SITE.barn.name} in ${SITE.barn.city}, Missouri.`}
  description="Information about dressage boarding and training board with Natalie Hammond at Paradiso Farm in Wentzville, Missouri, serving St. Louis and the surrounding area."
  keywords="dressage boarding, horse boarding, training board, st louis, saint louis, wentzville, st charles county, equestrian, horse"
  hero={hero}
  heroAlt="Natalie riding a grey horse at a dressage show"
  jsonLd={businessLd}
>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Natalie rides and trains out of <a href={SITE.barn.url} rel="noopener">{SITE.barn.name}</a> in
      {SITE.barn.city}, Missouri, a short drive from St. Louis, Wildwood, Chesterfield and St. Charles County.
    </p>
    <p>
      A dressage horse does best when daily care and training work together. If you're looking for boarding in the St.
      Louis area for a horse in full or partial training with Natalie, she can talk you through the current options and
      availability at {SITE.barn.name}.
    </p>

    <h2>Training with boarding</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Full training:</strong> regular training rides and lessons, with individual attention for your horse.</li>
      <li><strong>Partial training:</strong> a flexible mix of professional rides and your own lessons.</li>
      <li><strong>Lessons and show support:</strong> coaching for riders at every level, at home and at shows.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Natalie keeps a limited number of horses in training, so openings are limited. See the
      <a href="/training/">dressage training page</a> for more.
    </p>

    <h2>Ask about availability</h2>
    <p>
      For details on pricing and availability, please <a href="/contact/">contact Natalie</a>.
    </p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Contact Natalie</a></p>
  </div>
</Page>
